# Names a real, running local model "jarvis" inside Ollama, built on an
# existing open-weight base model (default: Gemma 3 — swap the FROM line
# for any other model already pulled, e.g. `llama3.1`, `qwen2.5`,
# `mistral`, `deepseek-r1`). This does NOT train a new model from
# scratch — that needs resources (data/compute/months of work) this
# project cannot provide, see docs/DECISIONS.md. It DOES make `ollama
# list` / `ollama run jarvis` show and run something named "jarvis", not
# the base model's name — a real, distinct model identity in Ollama's own
# registry, not just a system prompt pasted on top at request time.
#
# Usage:
#   ollama pull gemma3          # or whichever model you put in FROM below
#   ollama create jarvis -f agent/provider/ollama/Modelfile
#   ollama run jarvis           # now it's "jarvis", not "gemma3"
#
# The SYSTEM block below is a fallback identity for direct/interactive use
# (`ollama run jarvis` outside the backend). The real Jarvis backend
# already injects the full, current system prompt (prompts/system_prompt.md
# + live ContextEngine data) on every request regardless of this default —
# this Modelfile only controls what you get if you talk to "jarvis"
# directly through Ollama itself.

FROM gemma3

SYSTEM """
You are Jarvis, a personal AI assistant. Be direct and concise. Before
any sensitive action (sending a message, deleting data, spending money),
stop and ask for confirmation rather than proceeding on your own.
"""
